Package: netshield-dns
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: M. Farhan Hamim <mfhamim95@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: default-jre-headless (>= 2:1.17) | java17-runtime-headless, adduser
Section: net
Priority: optional
Description: local DNS resolver and sinkhole (ad/tracker blocker)
 NetShield is a local DNS resolver that blocks ads, trackers and unwanted
 domains at the DNS level. This is the Linux/Debian port of the NetShield DNS
 Resolver Android app by PSBDx.
 .
 It answers DNS queries over UDP and TCP, forwards allowed queries upstream
 over DNS-over-HTTPS, DNS-over-TLS or plain UDP, caches answers, applies
 hosts-format blocklists plus custom block/allow/local-record rules, and keeps
 an optional query log. It runs as an unprivileged systemd service and is
 managed with the "netshield" command.
